  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>At the end of the Verdon gorges, the Vinon-sur-Verdon lake offers a quieter and less spectacular alternative to Sainte-Croix — but also much less crowded at the height of summer, which makes it a good option for a dog that doesn't like crowds.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>This is mainly a local leisure lake, more modest than the big reservoir lakes of the Verdon, but it offers a genuine cool-down stop at the end of a trip through the gorges.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: handy if you're coming back from the Verdon gorges at the end of the day and want one last swim before hitting the road.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Manosque, a few minutes away, is a good stop for shops or a restaurant after the swim.</p>
